 # Durable Chorus room log + per-agent read cursors
-# Durable Chorus room log + per-agent read cursors
-
-Durable append-only Chorus room log (SQLite) + per-agent read cursors that survive abort/resume. This is the targeted slice that both kills the re-delivery bug (TAT-68) at its root and advances the accepted architectural north star, without committing to the full Broadcast MVP (TAT-10). Design is complete per the sizing spec at .sandpiper/docs/specs/durable-rooms-sizing.md — all 5 load-bearing OQs resolved (SQLite ratified, schema from current JSON + migrations, UUIDv7 post id + rowid seq cursor key, advance-on-success semantics, immutable append-only). Six implementation chunks (C1–C6); chunks 1–4 deliver the bug fix, even before the full nudge-demotion rewire.
+# Durable Tattler message log + per-agent read cursors
+
+Durable append-only Tattler message log (SQLite) + per-agent read cursors that survive abort/resume. While Chorus inspired this work, the durability primitive lives at the Tattler layer — Tattler owns the pipe and the persistence of that pipe. Chorus consumes the durable substrate for coordination semantics (broker, fanout, audience). This targeted slice both kills the re-delivery bug (TAT-68) at its root and advances the accepted architectural north star, without committing to the full Broadcast MVP (TAT-10). Design is complete per the sizing spec at .sandpiper/docs/specs/durable-rooms-sizing.md — all 5 load-bearing OQs resolved (SQLite ratified, schema from current JSON + migrations, UUIDv7 post id + rowid seq cursor key, advance-on-success semantics, immutable append-only). Six implementation chunks (C1–C6); chunks 1–4 deliver the bug fix, even before the full nudge-demotion rewire. NOTE: This scope covers the Tattler protocol layer only. A parallel TUI overhaul (decoupling from session-broker model, standalone TUI acceptable for MVP) is separate work to be sized independently.
 
